KNOWNBUG
array_element_part_select_lhs1.sv
--bound 2
^\[main\.p0\] always \(.*\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^unsupported lvalue
--
A part-select of an unpacked array element as the target of a
nonblocking assignment, e.g. mem[addr][7:0] <= wdata[7:0] (1800-2017
7.4.6, 11.5.1), is rejected by the RTL builder:

  unsupported lvalue for RTL construction: `verilog_non_indexed_part_select'
  CONVERSION ERROR

verilog_rtl_buildert::decompose_lhs (src/verilog/verilog_rtl.cpp) does
not handle a part-select whose operand is an index expression into an
array. This is the usual byte-enable memory write idiom, found in
picosoc_mem (picorv32/picosoc/picosoc.v).
